Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
21.3 Coupled to dirac16complex: the matter-dominated cubic regime and \
decompactification\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"1b7c0083-ad68-af41-8dbb-7143a74704d1"],

Cell["\<\
Now couple the gravity of section 21.2 to a gas of dirac16complex particles. \
In the primordial regime the mass and the self-couplings are negligible (m \
\[LessLess] Ha and g_r n^(6/7) \[LessLess] 1 with n the number density of the \
gas, i.e. (k_phys/M8)^6 \[LessLess] 1 for g_r \[TildeTilde] M8\:207b\:2076; \
section 23.3), so the Kohn\[Dash]Sham matter of section 16 reduces to a \
massless collisionless gas with an isotropic comoving momentum distribution \
(normalized so that a = b = 1 at Ha = 1, where its energy density is \[Kappa]\
\[Epsilon] = 10\:207b\:2076 \[Times] 3Ha\.b2): with the weight \
cos\.b2\[Theta] sin\.b3\[Theta] of the seven-dimensional momentum sphere,\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a9eed1c8-aa38-4946-ab41-39816162ee06"],

Cell["\<\
      \[Kappa]\[Epsilon] = C (a\.b3b\:2074)\:207b\.b9 \[LeftAngleBracket]\
\[Sqrt](cos\.b2\[Theta]/a\.b2 + sin\.b2\[Theta]/b\.b2)\[RightAngleBracket],   \
\[Kappa] pa = C (a\.b3b\:2074)\:207b\.b9 \
\[LeftAngleBracket]cos\.b2\[Theta]/(3a\.b2 \[Omega])\[RightAngleBracket],   \
\[Kappa] pb = C (a\.b3b\:2074)\:207b\.b9 \
\[LeftAngleBracket]sin\.b2\[Theta]/(4b\.b2 \[Omega])\[RightAngleBracket].\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a5d175c5-0659-ce44-877a-7cbf81867a55"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Matter-dominated cubic regime. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "Near \[Tau] = 0 any fluid with pa = w_a \[Epsilon] (w_a < 1) wins over the \
vacuum terms. With b finite and Ha = p/\[Tau] the leading 44 equation is \
p\.b3(p \[Minus] 1)(648\[Alpha]_3 h\.b2 \[Minus] 12\[Alpha]_2) = 0, so Hb \
\[RightArrow] h* = \[Minus]\[Sqrt](\[Alpha]_2/(54\[Alpha]_3)) (not h0), and \
the 11 and 00 equations give"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b9b08eb9-2ab9-b943-9b89-5164d7b82402"],

Cell["\<\
      p = 1/(1 + w_a),   \[Kappa] \[Epsilon] \[Tau]\.b3 \[RightArrow] (64/3) \
p\.b3 \[Alpha]_2 |h*|,   \[Alpha]_2E^(2) : \[Alpha]_3E^(3) : \[Kappa]\
\[Epsilon] \[RightArrow] 9/4 : \[Minus]5/4 : 1.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"548f4c25-ede5-f24e-973b-95073cceba71"],

Cell["\<\
For the gas (and for brane radiation) w_a \[RightArrow] 1/3 as a/b \
\[RightArrow] 0: a \[Proportional] \[Tau]^(3/4). The GAS FRACTION is \[Kappa]\
\[Epsilon] divided by the sum of the sizes of all terms of the 00 equation, \
S_1 + S_2 + S_3 + \[Kappa]\[Epsilon], where the size of a curvature term is \
the sum of the absolute values of its monomials in Ha and Hb: S_1 = 3(Ha\.b2 \
+ 4Ha|Hb| + 2Hb\.b2), S_2 = 12\[Alpha]_2|Hb|(4Ha\.b3 + 18Ha\.b2|Hb| + 12Ha Hb\
\.b2 + |Hb|\.b3), S_3 = 360\[Alpha]_3 Ha\.b2|Hb|\.b3(4Ha + 3|Hb|) (in a \
Kasner regime the monomials of the dominant term cancel each other, so its \
net value would hide it). Moving forward in time the gas fraction decreases \
in the cubic regime (\[Epsilon] \[Proportional] \[Tau]\:207b\:2074 against \
\[Tau]\:207b\.b3) and in the Gauss\[Dash]Bonnet regime (\[Epsilon] \
\[Proportional] \[Tau]^(\[Minus]4(p2+q2)) against \[Tau]\:207b\:2074), so the \
vacuum regimes of section 21.2 follow; in the Einstein regime it grows like \
\[Tau]^(2 \[Minus] 3p1 \[Minus] 5q1) = \[Tau]^1.160 (the auxiliary momenta \
are blue-shifted, pb \[RightArrow] \[Epsilon]/4, pa \[RightArrow] 0).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6bc8b87e-eff4-814f-a266-056ac697498f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Decompactification. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "Einstein gravity with a fluid pa = w_a \[Epsilon], pb = w_b \[Epsilon] has \
the power-law solutions a \[Proportional] \[Tau]^P, b \[Proportional] \
\[Tau]^Q with 3P(1 + w_a) + 4Q(1 + w_b) = 2: (w_a, w_b) = (0, 1/4) \
\[RightArrow] (P, Q) = (0, 2/5); (1/3, 0) \[RightArrow] (1/2, 0); (1/7, 1/7) \
\[RightArrow] (1/4, 1/4). Once the gas dominates, ordinary space stops \
expanding and the AUXILIARY SPACE EXPANDS, b \[Proportional] \[Tau]^(2/5): \
without the stabilizing potential U(b) the 7+1 universe decompactifies. \
Section 22.1 shows how U(b) prevents this."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"42dbd102-bb3c-3042-8492-f2e8bbab72e0"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Needs[\"NumericalDifferentialEquationAnalysis`\"];
rIgl = GaussianQuadratureWeights[128, 0, Pi/2, 30]; rIth = N[rIgl[[All, 1]]]; \
rIwt = N[rIgl[[All, 2]] Cos[rIgl[[All, 1]]]^2 Sin[rIgl[[All, 1]]]^3];
rIwt = rIwt/Total[rIwt]; rIc2 = Cos[rIth]^2; rIs2 = Sin[rIth]^2;
rIgas[la_?NumericQ, lb_?NumericQ] := Module[{ia2 = Exp[-2 la], ib2 = Exp[-2 \
lb], root, pref = Exp[-3 la - 4 lb]},
   root = Sqrt[rIc2 ia2 + rIs2 ib2]; pref {rIwt.root, rIwt.(rIc2 ia2/(3 \
root)), rIwt.(rIs2 ib2/(4 root))}];
rIC00[ha_, hb_] := rIc[[1]] /. {alf[2] -> 1, alf[3] -> rIxi, Ha -> ha, Hb -> \
hb};
rIlinM[ha_, hb_] := {{Coefficient[rIc[[2]], dHa], Coefficient[rIc[[2]], \
dHb]}, {Coefficient[rIc[[3]], dHa], Coefficient[rIc[[3]], dHb]}} /. {alf[2] \
-> 1, alf[3] -> rIxi, Ha -> ha, Hb -> hb};
rIlinB[ha_, hb_] := ({rIc[[2]], rIc[[3]]} /. {dHa -> 0, dHb -> 0}) /. {alf[2] \
-> 1, alf[3] -> rIxi, Ha -> ha, Hb -> hb};
rIlinMf = Function[{ha, hb}, Evaluate[rIlinM[ha, hb]]]; rIlinBf = \
Function[{ha, hb}, Evaluate[rIlinB[ha, hb]]];
rIsolve2[m_, v_] := {v[[1]] m[[2, 2]] - v[[2]] m[[1, 2]], m[[1, 1]] v[[2]] - \
m[[2, 1]] v[[1]]}/(m[[1, 1]] m[[2, 2]] - m[[1, 2]] m[[2, 1]]);   (* 2x2 \
Cramer rule *)
rIgasD[ha_?NumericQ, hb_?NumericQ, la_?NumericQ, lb_?NumericQ, cg_] := \
Module[{g = rIgas[la, lb]},
   rIsolve2[rIlinMf[ha, hb], -rIlinBf[ha, hb] - cg {g[[2]], g[[3]]}]];
rIgasRhs[sg_?NumericQ, yy_?VectorQ, cg_] := Module[{ha = Exp[-sg], d, dx},
   d = rIgasD[ha, yy[[1]], yy[[2]], yy[[3]], cg]; dx = -ha/d[[1]]; {d[[2]] \
dx, ha dx, yy[[1]] dx, dx}];
rICg = 10^-6 3; {rIhbVac1, rIx1} = rIvacAt[1];
rIhb1 = Hb /. FindRoot[rIC00[1, Hb] == rICg, {Hb, rIhbVac1}, WorkingPrecision \
-> 20];
rIcpl[smax_] := NDSolveValue[{rIyC'[sV] == rIgasRhs[sV, rIyC[sV], rICg], \
rIyC[0] == N[{rIhb1, 0, 0, rIx1}]}, rIyC, {sV, 0, smax},
    Method -> {\"ExplicitRungeKutta\", \"DifferenceOrder\" -> 8}, \
PrecisionGoal -> 12, AccuracyGoal -> 30, MaxSteps -> 10^6, InterpolationOrder \
-> All];
rIcplB = rIcpl[-Log[10^16]]; rIcplF = rIcpl[-Log[10^-14]];
rIxs = rIcplB[-Log[10^16]][[4]] - 3/4 10^-16;
rIstate[h_] := Module[{sol = If[h >= 1, rIcplB, rIcplF], hb, la, lb, x, g, d, \
e2, e3, sz, hm},
   {hb, la, lb, x} = sol[-Log[h]]; g = rIgas[la, lb]; d = rIgasD[h, hb, la, \
lb, rICg]; hm = Abs[hb];
   e2 = -12 hb (4 h^3 + 18 h^2 hb + 12 h hb^2 + hb^3); e3 = 360 rIxi h^2 hb^3 \
(4 h + 3 hb);
   sz = {3 (h^2 + 4 h hm + 2 hm^2), 12 hm (4 h^3 + 18 h^2 hm + 12 h hm^2 + \
hm^3), 360 rIxi h^2 hm^3 (4 h + 3 hm), rICg g[[1]]};   (* sizes S1, S2, S3, \
kappa eps *)
   <|\"Hb\" -> hb, \"tau\" -> x - rIxs, \"peff\" -> -h^2/d[[1]], \"keps\" -> \
rICg g[[1]], \"E2\" -> e2, \"E3\" -> e3, \"S\" -> sz, \"frac\" -> \
sz[[4]]/Total[sz],
     \"pa/e\" -> g[[2]]/g[[1]], \"pb/e\" -> g[[3]]/g[[1]]|>];
rIhStar = -1/Sqrt[54 rIxi];
rInear = rIstate[10^15];
check[\"matter-dominated cubic regime: p_eff -> 3/4, Hb -> -Sqrt[alpha2/(54 \
alpha3)], kappa eps tau^3 -> 9 alpha2 |h*|, alpha2 E2 : alpha3 E3 : kappa eps \
-> 9/4 : -5/4 : 1 (Ha = 10^15)\",
  Abs[rInear[\"peff\"] - 3/4] < 10^-3 && Abs[rInear[\"Hb\"]/rIhStar - 1] < \
10^-3 && Abs[rInear[\"keps\"] rInear[\"tau\"]^3/(9 Abs[rIhStar]) - 1] < 10^-2 \
&&
  Abs[rInear[\"E2\"]/rInear[\"keps\"] - 9/4] < 10^-2 && \
Abs[rInear[\"E3\"]/rInear[\"keps\"] + 5/4] < 10^-2]
rIplat = rIstate /@ {3 10^5, 30, 10^-2};
check[\"coupled: where the gas is a small fraction the effective exponents \
are those of the vacuum (1, p2, p1 within 10^-2)\",
  Abs[rIplat[[1]][\"peff\"] - 1] < 10^-2 && Abs[rIplat[[2]][\"peff\"] - rIp2] \
< 10^-2 && Abs[rIplat[[3]][\"peff\"] - rIp1] < 10^-2]
rIlate = rIstate[10^-14];
check[\"without the stabilizing potential the gas-dominated Einstein regime \
decompactifies: tau Ha -> 0, tau Hb -> 2/5, pb/eps -> 1/4 (Ha = 10^-14)\",
  rIlate[\"tau\"] 10^-14 < 10^-3 && Abs[rIlate[\"tau\"] rIlate[\"Hb\"] - 2/5] \
< 2 10^-3 && Abs[rIlate[\"pb/e\"] - 1/4] < 10^-3]
rIgrow = With[{gA = rIstate[10^-2], gB = rIstate[10^-4]}, \
Log[(gB[\"keps\"]/(3 10^-8))/(gA[\"keps\"]/(3 \
10^-4))]/Log[gB[\"tau\"]/gA[\"tau\"]]];
check[\"the gas fraction grows like tau^(2 - 3 p1 - 5 q1) = tau^1.160 in the \
Einstein regime (to 2 10^-2)\", Abs[rIgrow - (2 - 3 rIp1 - 5 rIq1)] < 2 10^-2]
rIfl[wa_, wb_] := Solve[{(3 (pP^2 + 4 pP qQ + 2 qQ^2)) == cC, (3 pP^2 + 8 pP \
qQ - 2 pP + 10 qQ^2 - 4 qQ) == -wa cC, 3 (2 pP^2 + 3 pP qQ - pP + 2 qQ^2 - \
qQ) == -wb cC,
     3 pP (1 + wa) + 4 qQ (1 + wb) == 2}, {pP, qQ, cC}];
check[\"Einstein + fluid power laws a ~ tau^P, b ~ tau^Q: (wa, wb) = (0, 1/4) \
-> (0, 2/5); (1/3, 0) -> (1/2, 0); (1/7, 1/7) -> (1/4, 1/4) (tau^2 E^(1) from \
EKas of section 14.1)\",
  Expand[(EKas[[1]] /. {pK -> pP, qK -> qQ}) - {3 (pP^2 + 4 pP qQ + 2 qQ^2), \
3 pP^2 + 8 pP qQ - 2 pP + 10 qQ^2 - 4 qQ, 3 (2 pP^2 + 3 pP qQ - pP + 2 qQ^2 - \
qQ)}] === {0, 0, 0} &&
  rIfl[0, 1/4] == {{pP -> 0, qQ -> 2/5, cC -> 24/25}} && rIfl[1/3, 0] == {{pP \
-> 1/2, qQ -> 0, cC -> 3/4}} && rIfl[1/7, 1/7] == {{pP -> 1/4, qQ -> 1/4, cC \
-> 21/16}}]
rIlead = {Coefficient[Expand[(rIc[[1]] /. {Ha -> pw/tS, Hb -> rIIIhh, dHa -> \
-pw/tS^2, dHb -> 0}) tS^3], tS, 0],
   Coefficient[Expand[(rIc[[2]] /. {Ha -> pw/tS, Hb -> rIIIhh, dHa -> \
-pw/tS^2, dHb -> 0}) tS^3], tS, 0],
   Coefficient[Expand[(rIc[[3]] /. {Ha -> pw/tS, Hb -> rIIIhh, dHa -> \
-pw/tS^2, dHb -> 0}) tS^4], tS, 0]};
check[\"matter-dominated cubic regime (any fluid, b finite): leading 44 term \
p^3 (p - 1)(648 alpha3 h^2 - 12 alpha2); with h^2 = alpha2/(54 alpha3): p = \
1/(1 + w_a) and kappa eps tau^3 = (64/3) p^3 alpha2 |h|\",
  Expand[rIlead[[3]] - pw^3 (pw - 1) (648 alf[3] rIIIhh^2 - 12 alf[2])] === 0 \
&&
  (Select[pw /. Solve[(rIlead[[2]] + wA rIlead[[1]] /. rIIIhh -> \
-Sqrt[alf[2]/(54 alf[3])]) == 0, pw], # =!= 0 &] // Simplify) == {1/(1 + wA)} \
&&
  Simplify[(rIlead[[1]] /. rIIIhh -> -Sqrt[alf[2]/(54 alf[3])]) - 64/3 pw^3 \
alf[2] Sqrt[alf[2]/(54 alf[3])], alf[2] > 0 && alf[3] > 0] === 0]
{\"near the singularity (Ha = 10^15): p_eff, Hb, kappa eps tau^3, alpha2 \
E2/(kappa eps), alpha3 E3/(kappa eps)\" -> {rInear[\"peff\"], rInear[\"Hb\"], \
rInear[\"keps\"] rInear[\"tau\"]^3, rInear[\"E2\"]/rInear[\"keps\"], \
rInear[\"E3\"]/rInear[\"keps\"]},
 \"(p_eff, gas fraction) at Ha = 3 10^5, 30, 10^-2\" -> ({#[\"peff\"], \
#[\"frac\"]} & /@ rIplat), \"late (Ha = 10^-14): tau Ha, tau Hb, pa/eps, \
pb/eps\" -> {rIlate[\"tau\"] 10^-14, rIlate[\"tau\"] rIlate[\"Hb\"], \
rIlate[\"pa/e\"], rIlate[\"pb/e\"]},
 \"Einstein-regime growth exponent: numerical, 2 - 3 p1 - 5 q1\" -> {rIgrow, \
N[2 - 3 rIp1 - 5 rIq1]}}\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[978]:=",ExpressionUUID->"72b2b3c4-449f-4f40-a638-92f182d92c00"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"matter-dominated cubic regime: p_eff -> 3/4, Hb -> \
